<title>USA: NY state Gov says will win approval of transit tax.</title>
<headline>NY state Gov says will win approval of transit tax.</headline>
<dateline>ALBANY, N.Y. 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York State Gov. George Pataki said on Tuesday he believed a special session of the legislature would approve an extension of a tax that helps pay for mass transit in 12 downstate counties.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe that we will be able to pass the Metropolitan Tranasportation Authority extender. We're not 100 percent there, but we're very close,&quot; the governor told reporters in Albany after meeting with top lawmakers, whom he recalled for the special session that began on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The transit tax was set to expire at year-end, along with a personal income tax surcharge for New York City, which the governor also forecast would be extended.</p>
<p>-- Joan Gralla, 212-859-1654</p>
